From 59dba3af73962b84d458296e0e95de52a0d5a3b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Roch=C3=A9=20Compaan?= <roche@upfrontsoftware.co.za>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:31:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] qwen35: dense recurrent SiLU output on CUDA

The dense graph's linear layers end in a per-head RMSNorm scaled by the
D-wide ssm_norm weights and gated by silu(z). Implement it as one warp per
head slice with D/32 contiguous elements per lane, the same mapping the Metal
kernel uses, and reuse the shared Qwen CUDA tensor, weight and launch helpers
from a new ds4_qwen35_cuda.cuh.

The test checks lengths 1, 8, 9, 17 and 256, head sizes 32, 64, 96 and 128,
zero and non-zero norm weights, and that the Qwen4 op still gates by
sigmoid(z). It also checks six refusals leave the output unchanged.

ds4_cuda.o now depends on ds4_qwen35_cuda.cuh; without that line a change to
the new header leaves a stale object file.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: dense qwen35 runs on CUDA upstream
Carried-commits: none (authored here)
